  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **No Children** (1 review): Darnielle tells the story behind the song once it finishes [7]\n- **I Am Morris Townsend** (1 review): Perry Wright sings this song, which is the nineteenth track [2]\n- **See America Right** (1 review): Darnielle forgets some of the lyrics during this song [7]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Golden Boy**: earliest performance in the archive; rare: 7 archived performances [8]\n- **You Better Keep It On Your Mind**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [8]\n- **Elijah**: back after 52 archived shows (1269 days) [8]\n- **Monkey In The Basement**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [8]\n- **Night Of The Mules**: back after 76 archived shows (3341 days); rare: 6 archived performances [8]\n- **I Am Morris Townsend**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [8]\n- Earliest performances in the archive: Jeff Davis County Blues [8]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **tmg2006-08-10.flac16** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 20 songs; 72 min; rated 4.67/5 by 6 [1]. Said about its sound: Reviewer calls the recording's quality excellent [2]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Darnielle is much chattier between songs than usual, apparently from drinking [2]\n- Darnielle sounds largely recovered from a cold he had at earlier shows [4]\n- An audience member tells Darnielle to stop his chatter; the reviewer describes the banter as slightly drunk [6]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **tmg2006-08-10.flac16**: taped by Sloan Simpson; transferred by Sloan Simpson; source: [Soundboard> Nomad Jukebox 3]+[Neumann KM-184(DIN)> Lunatec V2> Nomad Jukebox 3] [1]",
